  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving enforcement and establishing a rapid response team using SMART in the Nam Et-Phou Louey National Protect Area Landscape, LAO PDR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to provide highly informed and adaptive enforcement response in Nam Et-Phou Louey NPA through information-based patrolling, rapid response by foot patrols, and continuing enforcement efforts in key northern white-cheeked gibbon areas to obtain an inviolate core zone. This will be done by: (1) patrolling areas with known gibbon sign; (2) placing a rapid response patrol team directly into situations where threats to gibbons and their habitat are highest; (3) having all patrol teams collect data on gibbon sign in the protected area, feeding that information back to the newly installed SMART system, and then using that information to better understand which areas to concentrate enforcement efforts; (4) customizing the SMART data model to local needs; (5) translating the SMART interface into the Lao language; (6) training local SMART database operators in data input, management and analysis; and (7) making presentations to promote the SMART model to other protected areas. ..&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
